# {{ N.mcp }}.1) Get Access and the Server URLs

On this page, you'll install the local tools, collect the two values that make up the MCP server URLs, and confirm you have permission to call both servers.

## Task 1 - Install the local tools

1. Install the Databricks CLI if you don't have it yet. On macOS or Linux, run:

    ```bash
    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/databricks/setup-cli/main/install.sh | sh
    ```

    For Windows and other options, see [Install the Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/dev-tools/cli/install).

2. Sign in to your workspace. Replace `<workspace-hostname>` with the host in your browser's address bar (for example `dbc-1234abcd-5678.cloud.databricks.com`).

    ```bash
    databricks auth login --host https://<workspace-hostname> --profile {{ m.cli_profile }}
    ```

3. Create a Python 3.12 environment for this Step and install the packages:

    ```bash
    python3.12 -m venv .venv-mcp && source .venv-mcp/bin/activate
    pip install --upgrade databricks-sdk databricks-openai openai-agents "mcp>=1.24,<2"
    ```

## Task 2 - Find your Genie space ID

The Genie Agent MCP URL ends with the ID of your Genie Agent (its *space ID*).

1. Click **Genie Agents** in the left sidebar and open `<your_name> - {{ s.naming.agent }}`.

2. Copy the space ID. It is the 32-character value after `/rooms/` in your browser's address bar, and it is also shown in the agent's **Settings**.

    ```text title="Example"
    https://<workspace-hostname>/genie/rooms/01ef0123456789abcdef0123456789ab
    ```

3. Save it as an environment variable in your terminal:

    ```bash
    export GENIE_SPACE_ID=<your-space-id>
    ```

## Task 3 - Find your workspace ID

The Genie One MCP URL needs your **workspace ID** in the `o=` query parameter.

1. Run the following command. It prints the numeric workspace ID of the workspace you signed in to in Task 1.

    ```bash
    python -c "from databricks.sdk import WorkspaceClient; print(WorkspaceClient(profile='{{ m.cli_profile }}').get_workspace_id())"
    ```

    You can also find it as the `o=` value in your workspace URL.

## Task 4 - Confirm your access

1. **Genie Agent MCP.** You created the Genie Agent, so you can already call it. Anyone else (a teammate, or the service principal your product runs as) needs **Can Run** on the Genie Agent, `SELECT` on `{{ mv1.name }}` and `{{ mv2.name }}`, `USE CATALOG` and `USE SCHEMA` on `{{ cat }}.default`, and permission to use the Genie Agent's SQL warehouse. Share the Genie Agent with **Share** in its top-right corner.

2. **Genie One MCP.** Check that you have `EXECUTE` on the Databricks-provided MCP `system.ai.genie_one_mcp`. Replace the email with yours:

    ```bash
    databricks grants get-effective mcp_service system.ai.genie_one_mcp \
      --principal you@example.com --profile {{ m.cli_profile }}
    ```

3. Verify the output lists `EXECUTE`. In most workspaces it is inherited from the `system.ai` schema through the `account users` group, so `inherited_from_name` shows `system.ai`.

    !!! warning "No EXECUTE?"
        Ask your workspace admin to grant it. A metastore admin must first grant themselves `MANAGE` on the `system.ai` schema, then run `databricks grants update mcp_service system.ai.genie_one_mcp --json '{"changes": [{"principal": "you@example.com", "add": ["EXECUTE"]}]}'`. The securable type is `mcp_service`, not `function` or `mcp`.

## Task 5 - Write down your two server URLs

Fill in the values from Tasks 2 and 3. You'll use these URLs in {{ N.mcp }}.2 and {{ N.mcp }}.3.

| Server | URL |
|---|---|
| Genie Agent MCP | `https://<workspace-hostname>/api/2.0/mcp/genie/<space-id>` |
| Genie One MCP | `https://<workspace-hostname>/ai-gateway/mcp-services/system.ai.genie_one_mcp?o=<workspace-id>` |

!!! info "Older Genie MCP endpoint"
    If you find examples that use `https://<workspace-hostname>/api/2.0/mcp/genie` with no space ID, that is the deprecated Beta endpoint for Genie One. It stops working on November 30, 2026. Use the `system.ai.genie_one_mcp` URL above instead; the tool names are the same.

!!! success "Ready"
    You have the tools, both URLs and the permissions you need. Next, you'll connect them to a coding agent.
